========================================================
DOCKER INTERVIEW REVISION NOTES
BEGINNER TO DEVOPS LEVEL
========================================================

1. WHAT IS DOCKER?
------------------
Docker is a containerization platform used to package
applications and their dependencies together.

Benefits:
- Consistent environments
- Faster deployments
- Lightweight
- Portable

========================================================

2. IMAGE VS CONTAINER
---------------------

IMAGE
-----
- Blueprint/Template
- Read-only
- Used to create containers

Examples:
nginx
ubuntu
jenkins

CONTAINER
---------
- Running instance of image
- Executable environment

Example:

ubuntu image
      ↓
docker run
      ↓
ubuntu container

Interview Answer:
Image = Blueprint
Container = Running Instance

========================================================

3. CHECK DOCKER VERSION
-----------------------

docker --version

Purpose:
Verify Docker installation.

========================================================

4. LIST IMAGES
--------------

docker images

Purpose:
Show all downloaded images.

Output:
Repository
Tag
Image ID
Size

========================================================

5. DOWNLOAD IMAGE
-----------------

docker pull nginx

Purpose:
Download image from Docker Hub.

========================================================

6. RUN CONTAINER
----------------

docker run ubuntu

Purpose:
Create and start container.

Why container exits?
No foreground process running.

========================================================

7. INTERACTIVE CONTAINER
------------------------

docker run -it ubuntu bash

-i = Interactive
-t = Terminal

Purpose:
Enter container shell.

Output:

root@containerid:/#

========================================================

8. DETACHED MODE
----------------

docker run -d nginx

-d = Detached Mode

Purpose:
Run container in background.

========================================================

9. NAMED CONTAINER
------------------

docker run -d --name mynginx nginx

Purpose:
Give custom name to container.

========================================================

10. PORT MAPPING
----------------

docker run -d --name mynginx -p 8081:80 nginx

Meaning:

HOST PORT      CONTAINER PORT

8081     --->      80

Purpose:
Expose container application outside.

Access:

http://localhost:8081

========================================================

11. LIST RUNNING CONTAINERS
---------------------------

docker ps

Purpose:
Show running containers.

========================================================

12. LIST ALL CONTAINERS
-----------------------

docker ps -a

Purpose:
Show running + stopped containers.

========================================================

13. ENTER RUNNING CONTAINER
---------------------------

docker exec -it mynginx bash

Purpose:
Open shell inside running container.

========================================================

14. CONTAINER LOGS
------------------

docker logs mynginx

Purpose:
View container output/logs.

========================================================

15. STOP CONTAINER
------------------

docker stop mynginx

Purpose:
Gracefully stop container.

========================================================

16. START CONTAINER
-------------------

docker start mynginx

Purpose:
Start stopped container.

========================================================

17. RESTART CONTAINER
---------------------

docker restart mynginx

Purpose:
Stop and start container.

========================================================

18. REMOVE CONTAINER
--------------------

docker rm mynginx

Purpose:
Delete stopped container.

Force delete:

docker rm -f mynginx

========================================================

19. REMOVE IMAGE
----------------

docker rmi nginx

Purpose:
Delete image.

========================================================

20. INSPECT IMAGE
-----------------

docker image inspect nginx

Purpose:
Show image metadata.

Important Fields:

RepoTags
ExposedPorts
Env
Entrypoint
Cmd
Architecture
Layers

========================================================

21. INSPECT CONTAINER
---------------------

docker inspect mynginx

Purpose:
Show detailed container information.

========================================================

22. ENTRYPOINT
--------------

Example:

ENTRYPOINT ["nginx"]

Purpose:
Main executable started by container.

========================================================

23. CMD
--------

CMD ["-g","daemon off;"]

Purpose:
Default arguments for ENTRYPOINT.

Final Command:

nginx -g "daemon off;"

========================================================

24. DOCKERFILE
--------------

Used to build custom images.

Example:

FROM ubuntu

RUN apt update

CMD ["echo","Hello Docker"]

========================================================

25. BUILD IMAGE
---------------

docker build -t myapp .

-t = Tag

Purpose:
Create image from Dockerfile.

========================================================

26. RUN CUSTOM IMAGE
--------------------

docker run myapp

Purpose:
Run image created from Dockerfile.

========================================================

27. HOST VS CONTAINER
---------------------

HOST
----
Actual machine running Docker.

CONTAINER
---------
Isolated environment running application.

========================================================

28. WHY "docker: command not found"
-----------------------------------

Inside Ubuntu container:

docker run -it ubuntu bash

docker

Output:

docker: command not found

Reason:
Docker installed on host,
not inside container.

